{{!
    @template core/sticky_footer

    Displays a page sticky footer element (theme_sentientia override).

    Persona-pass fix D5 (2026-09-30). This theme is standalone (no parent
    theme), so it needs its own copy of the core sticky footer template.
    Without one, core's default template renders the element with no
    "stickyfooter" class, and the grader report's JS (gradereport_grader/
    stickycolspan) does a querySelector on that class, gets null and throws
    "Cannot read properties of null (reading offsetHeight)" on every
    gradebook view. Only a Boost override used to add the class.

    This copy is core's default markup plus the "stickyfooter" class, which is
    the hook that core/sticky-footer and the grader JS look for. It adds no
    positioning: the footer stays the in-flow card that the grade report
    styling in _surface-grade-report.scss already gives it (and core's
    v-hidden class hides it when a page asks for a disabled sticky footer).

    Classes required for JS:
    * stickyfooter - the element the sticky footer JS looks up

    Data attributes optional for JS:
    * data-disable Number|String - If the sticky footer should be disabled by default

    Context variables required for this template:
    * disable Boolean - if the sticky footer should be loaded hidden

    Example context (json):
    {
        "stickycontent" : "<a href=\"#\">Moodle</a>",
        "extras" : [
            {
                "attribute" : "data-example",
                "value" : "stickyfooter"
            }
        ],
        "stickyclasses" : "extraclasses"
    }
}}
<div
    id="sticky-footer"
    class="stickyfooter {{$ stickyclasses }}{{stickyclasses}}{{/ stickyclasses }}"
    {{$ disable }}
        {{#disable}} data-disable="true" {{/disable}}
    {{/ disable }}
    {{#extras}}
    {{attribute}}="{{value}}"
    {{/extras}}
>
    {{$ stickycontent }}
        {{{stickycontent}}}
    {{/ stickycontent }}
</div>
{{#js}}
require(['core/sticky-footer'], function(footer) {
    footer.init();
});

{{/js}}
